How heavily spoiled do you want to be ?

Level 1:
There is a level in Gehennom with *no* stairs down. You're near the end
(of Gehennom at least).

And you can't dig down through this level but there is a way to create a
stair down and reach the deepest level of the game (yes, really, the
deepest).









Level 2:
To open the stairs, you need to perform a specific ritual, involving three
major artefacts in the game, at a specific place in the level.












Level 3:
The specific place is called "vibrating square". It's a non-wall square of
the last level and you'll get a special message (can't remember which)
when walking on it (drop something to remember its position). There is no
other way to find it than test (almost) every square.

The three artefacts are those you got from your quest nemesis, Vlad and
the Wizard.

The ritual consist of making some light (you still have 7 candles at hand,
don't you ?), ring to wake up the audience and then read your part (with
my luck, I'm probably wrong in the order, well just go with a few tries if
needed).


Keep going, you're close to the ascencion run (and next to the ascencion,
hopefully) !




Level 4:
Once you'll clean the last level (Moloch's sanctum), you'll have to go all
the way up (and more) to bring the amulet to your god. Once you've killed
the Wizard, he'll show up from time to time and be a real pain.
So, if you still haven't killed Rodney, you may wish to shorten the run.
In order to do so, dig straight paths from stairs to stairs in every
single level of the dungeon before going up.





Level 5:
In the endgame part (5 special levels outside of the dungeon), you'll need
a safe and quick way to find magic portal (traps). Be sure to carry either
a crystal ball with enough charges or cursed gold detection scrolls or
gold detection and a quick way to get confused/unconfused.

